<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zarpanitu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zarpanitu was a Babylonian goddess, the consort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marduk">Marduk</a>, the chief god of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. Her statue stood with his in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esagila">Esagila</a> temple. The Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mursili-i">Mursili I</a>, sacking Babylon, carried off the statues of Marduk and Zarpanitu, a raid that fatally destabilised the First Babylonian dynasty.</p></div>
